{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeSandwichReduces","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SymmetricGroupTowerWitness"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances.heckeTower_tr_mul_unconditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances.heckeTower_tr_mul_unconditional","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidedTowerInstances.lean#L288-L296","doc":"The same fact in the form that makes the degeneracy unmissable: for this\nwitness the trace law holds for **arbitrary** `a` and `b`, with no hypothesis\nabout levels, so `disjointBlock_heckeTower` is an instance of it and carries no\ndisjoint-block information. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances.towerTrace_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances.towerTrace_mul","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidedTowerInstances.lean#L281-L286","doc":"**Hence the presented tower's trace is an algebra homomorphism**, since\n`collapse` is one and `towerTrace = ocneanuTrace ∘ collapse`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances.ocneanuTrace_mul_of_markov","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances.ocneanuTrace_mul_of_markov","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidedTowerInstances.lean#L270-L279","doc":"**The Markov hypothesis makes the rank-2 Ocneanu trace multiplicative.**\n\n`HeckeRankTwoMarkov.ocneanuTrace_mul_defect` computes the defect on `σ · σ` as\n`h * z + 1 - z * z`; this shows the defect vanishes on *every* pair precisely\nunder `z * z = h * z + 1`, which is the Markov condition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances.sandwichReduces_sym_via_relations","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances.sandwichReduces_sym_via_relations","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidedTowerInstances.lean#L245-L253","doc":"**`SandwichReduces` on the symmetric-group tower, derived from the\nrelations** rather than from the permutation model.\n\n`SymmetricGroupTowerWitness.sandwichReduces_sym` is the same statement proved by\nsupport arguments through the double coset. Two independent routes to one\nconclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances.braidedTower_sym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances.braidedTower_sym","kind":"instance","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidedTowerInstances.lean#L235-L243","doc":"**The symmetric-group algebra tower is a `BraidedTower`**, with `h = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances.s_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances.s_braid","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidedTowerInstances.lean#L212-L231","doc":"**The braid relation for adjacent transpositions**: both sides are\n`swap m (m+2)`. Each is a conjugation of one swap by the other, computed with\n`Equiv.swap_apply_apply` and the involution `(s j)⁻¹ = s j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances.s_far","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances.s_far","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidedTowerInstances.lean#L201-L210","doc":"Distant adjacent transpositions commute. Conjugating `swap m (m+1)` by\n`s k` fixes both endpoints when `k + 1 < m`, so the conjugation is trivial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances.disjointBlock_heckeTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances.disjointBlock_heckeTower","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidedTowerInstances.lean#L183-L190","doc":"**The disjoint-block trace law on a Hecke tower with `h` unconstrained.**\n\n🛑 The trace here is the collapse-and-Ocneanu functional of `HeckeTowerWitness`,\nwhich is not faithful; this is not a statement about the Ocneanu trace of\n`H_∞(q)`. See the file docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances.towerSpan_heckeTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances.towerSpan_heckeTower","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidedTowerInstances.lean#L177-L181","doc":"**`TowerSpan` on the presented Hecke tower**, at any `h` — including the\nHecke case `h = q - q⁻¹ ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances.braidedTower_heckeTower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTowerInstances.braidedTower_heckeTower","kind":"instance","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidedTowerInstances.lean#L169-L175","doc":"**The presented infinite Hecke tower is a `BraidedTower`.** The three class\nfields are the three relations `RingQuot` imposes, verbatim. ","signatureChunk":0}]}